    {
      "id": "claim_1972d38a19914f12940dce22cb4ba951",
      "statement": "`list_tables` row counts are `reltuples` planner estimates rather than counts, and have been wrong here by whole orders of magnitude (a table reporting 0 held 16 rows), so a table can never be called empty on that number; a real `count(*)` requires an `execute_sql` permission ask.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://supabase/migrations/README.md#L33-L37",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cf628c7db15822a0b4e1032879fe3766feaae98e51aff19149de21abb8be6ee0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_522dd2d1c20e49b1899208c0090892d7",
      "statement": "Confirming that a specific migration landed means checking its objects by name in `pg_proc` for functions and `pg_policies` for policies; comparing policy sets is unreliable because several migrations add policies to the same tables, so a set comparison returns a superset that reads as a match no matter what is missing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://supabase/migrations/README.md#L39-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6adf0e5dd740d19fe8d2f9faec6378d785d719b85bbfa894b28729450299cb2b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f0c1f476ba744f91b08c98923d3e4d4d",
      "statement": "Because Supabase keys applied migrations on the version string, a recorded version that matches no filename makes `db push` re-run a file against a database that already has its objects; the standing fix is to record first and then name the file for the version actually recorded, and because `apply_migration` assigns its own version a file written with a guessed timestamp is renamed by reality.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://supabase/migrations/README.md#L77-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b3e695c98bb81537ba008cb99aba11685ad2400848b55539d7d80c9f5be34488:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://supabase/migrations/README.md#L8-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d410fbb17e3da8139abb82c8989c59072289197da0b3efbd576e04845261a1a2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_86460d5d25b94ba596df1ce099f9478e",
      "statement": "A `-- Active: <connection string>` header is the marker a SQL editor writes when a buffer is executed against a live connection, so it flags hand-execution that recorded nothing; two migration files carry one, each with two header lines.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://supabase/migrations/20260906114735_add_school_registry_and_platform_admin.sql#L1-L2",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:95ad35ea21260c07acd8ef60f747cf7bc3e301db1f61548a398ef37ad5d8796b:"
