    {
      "id": "claim_f73aebe9eabe4bb6a7bccd41033a1aaa",
      "statement": "Guarding every statement so a re-run is a no-op is the other half of the additive rule: `20261024071359` uses `add column if not exists` / `drop column if exists` and survives a replay, whereas `20261111120000` creates a table, trigger and policies with two bare `add constraint`s and is not re-runnable — which is why its objects were (re)created from an idempotent script instead of re-running the file; `20260910120000` likewise declares itself single-shot.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://supabase/migrations/20260910120000_add_adr001_billing_domain.sql#L49-L62",
